From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 7 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: use duelist helpers in processor.cpp (part 2)

Part 2 covers processor.cpp from calculate_battle_damage to the end of process(AddChain) step 8 (line 2933 to 3992 of the tree after patch 4).

Changed:
- 4 loops over duelists now use n_duelists (two battle damage effect loops, the turn step 0 reset loop, the second battle phase loop).
- 64 "1 - x" sites (57 lines) now use opponent_of. The x values are pa, pd and damp (controllers of cards on the field, or 0 or 1), one handler player, and one triggering player that goes into a uint8_t parameter.
- 1 turn player switch (Turn step 20) now uses next_in_turn_order.
- 5 local arrays (reflect twice, also twice, dp) now have size MAX_DUELISTS. The initial values are the same (all zero or false).
- 5 explicit pairs (battle damage reset, dp damage set, dp double damage, counter reset lambda, spsummon counter reset) are now loops over n_duelists in the same order.

With 2 duelists all of these give the same values in the same order. opponent_of returns uint8_t, and each site uses the value as an array index, a uint8_t argument or a compare with a uint8_t.

Left unchanged (listed in unchanged-sites.md):
- 3 sites with 1 - sumplayer (uint32_t, decision needed).
- 4 PLAYER_ALL / PLAYER_NONE sites (phase 2).
- 1 native tag mode site (tag_swap).
- 2 two-player pierce logic lines and the bd flags (relative, not per duelist).
